# This directory is a working area full of clones, logs, and scratch.
# Track ONLY the issue→PR cron's own config. Ignore everything else by default.
/*

# ...but keep the cron config + its docs:
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/campaign-run.sh
!/campaign-prompt.txt
# The standing brief `--agents` loads into every DISPATCHED worker. Tracked as PLAIN TEXT and
# wrapped into JSON by the runner, so it stays a prompt a human diffs rather than an escaped
# string literal — and so the conformance tests can grep it the way they grep the two prompts.
!/campaign-worker-prompt.txt
!/campaign-settings.json
!/cron.env.example
# weekly-budget pace gate (pre-flight called by both runners):
!/pr-review-report.sh
# Rust rewrite of pr-review-report.sh (target/ ignored by the project's own .gitignore):
!/pr-review-report-rs/
!/review-run.sh
# The vetter runs on the FSM MCP surface only (issue #52): prompt, tool allow/deny, server config.
!/review-prompt.txt
!/review-settings.json
!/review-mcp.json
# Producer's clone-lifecycle MCP surface (additive; the producer keeps its Bash):
!/campaign-mcp.json
# The human's own FSM transitions as a restricted surface, for an agent acting on
# the human's behalf (#86). No cron runs it; it is pointed at with --mcp-config.
!/human-mcp.json
!/merge-run.sh
!/merge-prompt.txt
!/merge-settings.json
# PreToolUse hooks (deploy to the box's claude hooks dir + wire in settings.json):
!/hooks/
!/hooks/block-nix-wrap-gh.sh
!/hooks/block-cron-git-bypass.sh
# The Claude Code marketplace this repo publishes, and the plugin it serves: the human's
# FSM transitions as slash commands (#94). Installed with `/plugin marketplace add
# rainlanguage/issue-pr-cron`, so these two must be TRACKED — an installer reads them
# from the repo, not from this box. `plugin-version-lockstep` gates their two versions.
!/.claude-plugin/
!/plugins/

# NEVER track the real deployment env (it holds the account handle / box-specific values):
/cron.env

# Explicitly NOT tracked (transient/operational/scratch), even if patterns change:
#   campaign.log, runs/, close-candidates.jsonl, DISABLED, *.lock  (runtime state)
#   WORKLOG.md, PRECOMPACT-SNAPSHOT.md                              (assistant scratch)
#   <repo> clones, ci-*/ rt-*/ fix-*/ etc.                          (work dirs)
!/sort-review-queue.sh
!/ORG-REGISTRY.md
# Producer QA doctrine (referenced by campaign-prompt step 4 + review-prompt QA gate):
!/QA-GUIDE.md
# Rust workspace + CI (rainix rust reusables gate pr-review-report):
!/Cargo.toml
!/Cargo.lock
!/.github/
!/.github/workflows/rust.yml
# Mutation-test scan records (committed so org health-checks can see scan freshness):
!/mutation-test-scans.json
# Per-run pipeline metrics (accumulates across trace rotation; committed periodically):
!/metrics/
!/metrics/runs.jsonl
# FSM-conformance snapshot (`pr-review-report human-queue --json`, overwritten each refresh);
# the rain-org-health dashboard fetches it at runtime from the raw URL — no site redeploy:
!/human-queue.json
!/refresh-human-queue.sh
# The design lane's FSM doctor (#241): daily pass routing every noQuestion ai:design PR back
# to ai:needs-work; a flake runner like the refresher, on its own cron line:
!/design-doctor.sh
# Append-only per-state inventory history ({ts, counts} per changed refresh) + its one-time
# backfill; the dashboard fetches the jsonl at runtime for the Theory-of-Constraints panel:
!/human-queue-history.jsonl
!/backfill-human-queue-history.sh
# Flake exposing pr-review-report as a package (bin on the cron PATH):
!/flake.nix
!/flake.lock

# worklist read-through cache (tool-local, regenerated each run)
.worklist-cache.json
